<figure class="post__image post__image--center"><img decoding="auto" loading="lazy"  src="https://pixelnostalgia.github.io/media/posts/356/jkdf2_logo.png" alt="" width="400" height="110" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" srcset="https://pixelnostalgia.github.io/media/posts/356/responsive/jkdf2_logo-xs.webp 300w ,https://pixelnostalgia.github.io/media/posts/356/responsive/jkdf2_logo-sm.webp 480w ,https://pixelnostalgia.github.io/media/posts/356/responsive/jkdf2_logo-md.webp 768w ,https://pixelnostalgia.github.io/media/posts/356/responsive/jkdf2_logo-xl.webp 1200w"></figure>
<figure class="post__image post__image--right"><img decoding="auto" loading="lazy"  src="https://pixelnostalgia.github.io/media/posts/356/jkdf2.png" alt="" width="1080" height="1080" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" srcset="https://pixelnostalgia.github.io/media/posts/356/responsive/jkdf2-xs.webp 300w ,https://pixelnostalgia.github.io/media/posts/356/responsive/jkdf2-sm.webp 480w ,https://pixelnostalgia.github.io/media/posts/356/responsive/jkdf2-md.webp 768w ,https://pixelnostalgia.github.io/media/posts/356/responsive/jkdf2-xl.webp 1200w"></figure>
<p> </p>
<p>OpenJKDF2 is a function-by-function reimplementation of Jedi Knight: Dark Forces II in C, with 64-bit ports to Windows 7+, macOS 10.15+, and Linux. Files are organized as closely to the original game as possible, based on symbols from the Grim Fandango Remaster Android/Linux/macOS port, as well as scattered assertions from various other games. It also contains the original versions of byacc and flex used for COG script parsing.</p>
<p>OpenJKDF2 added quality of life improvements to the game. This means it makes it easy to run Jedi Knight on modern machines with modern aspect ratios, monitor sizes, current generation graphic cards, and operating systems. It also now natively supports JKGFXMod—all of this simply by placing the contents of a zip file into your Jedi Knight directory!</p>

<h5>The package includes:</h5>
<p class="msg msg--success">2 games (~1,2 GB)</p>
